<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n13049" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπόλεμος</span></b> , 
			Ep.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπτόλεμος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>unwarlike,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. καὶ ἄναλκις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					2.201
				</span></i>
			, al., cf. <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Cyr.</u>
				7.4.1
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Jul.
				<u>Or.</u>
				2.87a
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. χειρὶ λείψεις βίον,</span>
			i.e. by <i>a woman's</i> hand, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Hec.</u>
				1034
			</span></i> (lyr.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>unwarlike, peaceful,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐνομία</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>P.</u>
					5.66
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐναί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Med.</u>
					640
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡσυχία</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.H.
					2.76
				</span></i>
			, etc. Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-μως, ἴσχειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Plt.</u>
					307e
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>invincible,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Ag.</u>
				768
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ch.</u>
				55
			</span></i> (lyr.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πόλεμος ἀ.</span> a war <i>that is no
				war,</i> a hopeless struggle, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Pr.</u>
				904
			</span></i> (lyr.) (Dind. metri gr. proposes <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπολέμιστος</span>), <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>HF</u>
				1133
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
